Z||000000||FieroHarry||07-14-2001||08:44 PM||||Okay,<BR>Ive spent 2 hours every night after work, making this thing come out the way I want before the Nationals....<BR>First my girlfriend put the bug in for me to get started, then one of my buddys found the hood for me.<BR>A couple of friends helped me do some of the work also, first we sanded down the nasty old red.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/one_1.jpg">  <BR>Then the scoops were marked out on top of the hood then we cut out the top sheet,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/two.jpg">  <BR>Add some resin to smooth them in,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/four.jpg">  <BR>the some glazing putty and primer and late last night a test coat of white to better veiw the final touches.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/eight.jpg[/img][img]http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/five.jpg[/img][img]http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seven.jpg">  [img]http://www.fiero.nl/uplo ads/six.jpg[/img]<BR>So what do you all think, am I crazy?<BR>I even got the RAM AIR hood sticker's from Pontiac to go on it and yes, its functional...<P>So whats the general opinion?<P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 266K+ <I>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA</I><BR><B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B><p>[This message has been edited by FieroHarry (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||14
